  "title": "RDS read replica or Aurora Replica",
  "claim": "An RDS read replica keeps its own copy and receives each change later; an Aurora Replica reads the writer's own volume.",
  "alt": "Two panels. RDS read replica: the application writes to the primary, which has its own storage; changes go asynchronously to a read replica with its own storage, and reports read the replica. Aurora: the application writes to the writer, the writer and two Aurora Replicas all connect to one shared cluster volume, and reports read the replicas through the reader endpoint.",
